            <div xml:id="d74">

                <pb facs="0203" n="107" sameAs="frus:frus1926v02/pg107"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.51 W 89France/411: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Whitehouse</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-10-20T16:00:00+00:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 20,
                                1926—4 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 5:02 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>388. Parliament will probably not be convoked until the second week in November,
                    it now appears, and will take up the budget <pb facs="0204" n="108"
                        xml:id="pg108"/> after ratifying the administrative reforms. Poincaré wishes
                    to have the budget voted before the beginning of the new year in order to avoid
                    provisional twelfths which dislocate budget provisions.</p>
                <p>Hostility to the ratification of the debt agreements without safeguard clause is
                    general and it has become apparent that reservations in a preamble would be
                    futile. It seems likely, therefore, that an attempt to reopen negotiations with
                    our Government will be made or at least there will be much delay in bringing the
                    agreements before Parliament.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Whitehouse</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
